+### Passing provider-specific parameters
+
+Different model providers sometimes have unique parameters that are not covered by the standard
+`ModelSettings` fields. `ModelSettings` accepts an `extra_args` dictionary of arbitrary keyword
+arguments that are passed straight through to the underlying model API call, so you can use
+provider-specific features without waiting for official support.
+
+```python
+from agents import Agent, ModelSettings
+
+english_agent = Agent(
+    name="English agent",
+    instructions="You only speak English",
+    model="gpt-4o",
+    model_settings=ModelSettings(
+        temperature=0.1,
+        extra_args={"some_provider_specific_arg": True},
+    ),
+)
+```
+
+!!! note
+
+    Not all model providers support all parameters, so passing unsupported parameters may cause
+    errors. Please check the API documentation for the specific model and provider you are
+    using. Any `None` values in `extra_args` are filtered out before the request is made, and
+    when model settings are merged (for example, agent settings combined with `RunConfig`
+    settings), the `extra_args` dictionaries are merged together with the more specific settings
+    taking precedence.
+
